  "answer": "**Verdict**\nFor Nomex in microgravity:\n- **ISS cabin** preset (14.7 psia, 21% O₂): Nomex is non-flammable at 21% O₂ across all evaluated ventilation flows (minimum O₂ limit is 24.1%).\n- **Artemis Exploration Atmosphere** preset (8.2 psia, 34% O₂): Nomex is flammable at 34% O₂ across a wide range of flow velocities (1–40 cm/s), with a minimum O₂ limit of 25.8%.\n\n**Key numbers**\n- **ISS cabin**: 21% O₂ at 14.7 psia (101.4 kPa). Minimum O₂ limit for burning ranges from 24.1% (at 8 cm/s flow) to 33.1% (at 0.5 cm/s flow). At 21% O₂, the material is below the flammability boundary at all flows.\n- **Artemis Exploration Atmosphere**: 34% O₂ at 8.2 psia (56.5 kPa). Minimum O₂ limit ranges from 25.8% (at 8–10 cm/s flow) to 34.9% (at 0.5 cm/s flow). Because 34% O₂ is above the minimum limit, Nomex burns at flows from 1 to 40 cm/s.\n\n**Evidence**\n- ISS cabin nearest experiments: `MOCK-SAFFIRE-06`, `MOCK-BASS-II-21`, `MOCK-BASS-II-03`.\n- Artemis atmosphere nearest experiments: `MOCK-BASS-II-24`, `MOCK-BASS-II-18`, `MOCK-BASS-II-12`.\n\n**Operational recommendation**\nWhen transitioning to the higher-oxygen Artemis atmosphere (8.2 psia, 34% O₂), treat Nomex as flammable. Implement strict controls: limit exposed material amounts, isolate potential ignition sources, ensure fire detection and suppression systems are ready, and consider lower O₂ operational limits where mission parameters allow.\n\n**Limits**\n- This is decision support, not a replacement for NASA-STD-6001 material testing.\n- The numbers come from a placeholder model (`mock_api`), not NASA data.",
